
  Background:
    Given a Databricks environment with PySpark setup
    And d_product_revenue table exists with invoice_number column

  Scenario: Drop the d_product_revenue_clone table if it exists
    Given d_product_revenue_clone table exists
    When the table is dropped
    Then d_product_revenue_clone table should not exist

  Scenario: Create a replica of d_product_revenue table in d_product_revenue_clone table
    Given d_product_revenue table exists
    When a replica of d_product_revenue is created in d_product_revenue_clone
    Then d_product_revenue_clone should have the same structure as d_product_revenue

  Scenario: Mask the last 4 digits of invoice_number in d_product_revenue_clone
    Given d_product_revenue_clone table is available
    And invoice_number column contains numeric values with at least 10 digits
    When last 4 digits of invoice_number are replaced with '****'
    Then invoice_number in d_product_revenue_clone should end with '****'
    Examples:
      | invoice_number  | masked_invoice_number |
      | 1234234534      | 123423****            |
      | 9876543210      | 987654****            |

  Scenario: Handle error when invoice_number is less than 10 digits
    Given invoice_number has less than 10 digits
    When the masking logic is applied
    Then an error condition should trigger with message "Invalid invoice_number format"
    Examples:
      | invoice_number |
      | 12345          |
      | 6789           |

  Scenario: Ensure data type consistency
    Given invoice_number is numeric
    When masked
    Then ensure the data type remains consistent with pre-masking format

  Scenario Outline: Test multiple invoice_number formats
    Given invoice_number with <format> format
    When masked
    Then invoice_number should end with '****'
    Examples:
      | format | invoice_number  | masked_invoice_number |
      | numeric | 1111222233      | 111122****            |
      | numeric | 4444555566      | 444455****            |
